{"qid":"Q156112","names":["Yue"],"title":"Yue","endonym":null,"capsule":"Yue was a powerful state of the Spring and Autumn and early Warring States periods, centered in present-day Zhejiang around its capital at Kuaiji. Under King Goujian it famously defeated the rival state of Wu around 473 BCE and briefly dominated the lower Yangtze. It was conquered and absorbed by the state of Chu around 334 BCE, scattering its royal house southward.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. This polity has not yet received individual source review: treat extents as indicative atlas convention.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":"topic/ecumenism","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Yue (state)","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"King Yunchang of Yue","nativeName":"越王允常","roman":"Yuè Wáng Yǔncháng","start":-537,"end":-497,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Goujian of Yue","nativeName":"越王勾踐","roman":"Yuè Wáng Gōujiàn","start":-496,"end":-465,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Lujian (Shiyu) of Yue","nativeName":"越王鹿郢","roman":"Yuè Wáng Lùyǐng","start":-464,"end":-459,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Bushou of Yue","nativeName":"越王不壽","roman":"Yuè Wáng Bùshòu","start":-458,"end":-449,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Zhugou of Yue","nativeName":"越王朱勾","roman":"Yuè Wáng Zhūgōu","start":-448,"end":-412,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Yi of Yue","nativeName":"越王翳","roman":"Yuè Wáng Yì","start":-411,"end":-376,"image":null,"imageUrl":n